  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "Salih: no motif. The she-camel is not drawn and its origin is not glossed (Al-Muyassar's «من الصخرة» is a report, not in the verse). Geometric for «اعبدوا الله», a house and a mountain for «قصورا… الجبال بيوتا». STAGING v4: Salih is a blue drop labelled Salih (no motif on his name); Thamud's people three faceless men in dark robes in a mountain valley (As-Sa'di: they lived in al-Hijr and around it; 74: houses carved in the mountains). c1 (73): Salih speaks (73:5), geometric on 73:7-13 (worship Allah), the camera on them for the clear proof (73:16); the she-camel stands beside Salih from the start, apart from the people (a camel actor; how she came out is not drawn, it is a report in Al-Muyassar only, and nothing on the miracle words); the camera on her for leave her to eat (73:24); wide for do not touch her with harm (nobody moves toward her); the camera on them for the painful punishment (73:32). c2 (74): the camel is not on this stage; Salih speaks (74:1); the camera on them (successors after 'Ad); house plate for the palaces on the plains (74:13-15), mountain plate for the houses carved in the mountains (74:16-17), light plate for the favours of Allah (74:19-20, not starting on the Name); the camera on them for do not spread corruption (74:21)."
